    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d479">

                <pb facs="0478" n="468" xml:id="pg468"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00116 European War 1939/1074: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Argentina</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Reed</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                            Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Buenos Aires</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-09-01">September 1,
                        1943</date>.<lb/>[Received September 1—11:17 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1997. Department’s 1132, 13th [<hi rendition="#italic">30th</hi>].<anchor n="16"
                        xml:id="d479-f1"/> Foreign Office made public last evening text of reply to
                    British note regarding war criminal refugees. Communiqué stated similar reply
                    made to this Embassy but we have not yet received it.<anchor n="17"
                        xml:id="d479-f2"/> Note states in substance that Argentine Government
                    distinguishes between common crimes and political offenses; that it holds asylum
                    should be granted only in case of political offense and that it will decide
                    accordingly each case that may be presented. Note is couched in courteous terms
                    and is accompanied by explanatory communiqué. Full text by mail.<anchor n="18"
                        xml:id="d479-f3"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Reed</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d479-f1" n="16" xml:id="d479-f1-content">
                <p>See footnote 5, <ref target="#pg461">p. 461</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d479-f2" n="17" xml:id="d479-f2-content">
                <p>Copy of reply transmitted to the Department by the Chargé in Argentina in his
                    despatch No. 11722, September 1.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d479-f3" n="18" xml:id="d479-f3-content">
                <p>Copy of translation of the Foreign Office communiqué published in <hi
                        rendition="#italic">La Nación</hi>, September 1, 1943, transmitted to the
                    Department by the Chargé in Argentina in his despatch No. 11795, September
                    4.</p>
            </note>
